{"_doc":"Idioms of this series for this learning language (scripts/notes.py from scripts/idioms/<series>[_deck].txt). lem = lexicon keys (lowercase, space separated) matched in a row against gloss tokens; t = shown form; ko/en = short meaning; note_ko/note_en = optional one-line note; n = letters it appears in; first = [letter id, message index]. Patterns win over idioms, idioms over anchors.","lang":"de","checked":false,"idioms":[{"lem":"gott lob","t":"Gott Lob","ko":"다행히, 하느님 덕분에","en":"thank God","n":3,"first":["c1-l2",0]},{"lem":"gott lob und dank","t":"Gott Lob und Dank","ko":"하느님께 감사하게도","en":"thank God","n":2,"first":["c1-l2",0]},{"lem":"von ganz herz","t":"von ganzem Herzen","ko":"진심으로","en":"with all my heart","n":3,"first":["c1-l1",0]},{"lem":"von herz","t":"von Herzen","ko":"진심으로","en":"from the heart","n":3,"first":["c3-l6",1]},{"lem":"auf dieser art","t":"auf diese Art","ko":"이런 식으로","en":"in this way","n":1,"first":["c4-l2",4]},{"lem":"nach haus","t":"nach Haus","ko":"집으로","en":"home(wards)","n":3,"first":["c1-l6",4]},{"lem":"zu haus","t":"zu Hause","ko":"집에","en":"at home","n":1,"first":["c7-l7",2]},{"lem":"in der tat","t":"in der That","ko":"정말로","en":"indeed","n":1,"first":["c6-l6",3]},{"lem":"über alle","t":"über Alles","ko":"무엇보다","en":"above all","n":1,"first":["c5-l2",3]},{"lem":"nach und nach","t":"nach und nach","ko":"조금씩","en":"little by little","n":1,"first":["c8-l2",3]},{"lem":"gar nicht","t":"gar nicht","ko":"전혀 ~않다","en":"not at all","n":2,"first":["c7-l5",0]},{"lem":"so viel","t":"so viele","ko":"그만큼","en":"so much","n":2,"first":["c2-l4",4]},{"lem":"so gut","t":"so gut","ko":"그렇게 잘, ~만큼","en":"as well as","n":2,"first":["c7-l1",4]},{"lem":"so wie","t":"so wie","ko":"~처럼","en":"just as","n":2,"first":["c4-l1",4]},{"lem":"eben so","t":"eben so","ko":"똑같이","en":"just as","n":1,"first":["c4-l6",4]},{"lem":"unrecht haben","t":"Unrecht habe","ko":"틀리다","en":"to be wrong","n":1,"first":["c4-l4",4]},{"lem":"in gott name","t":"in Gottes Namen","ko":"하느님의 이름으로, 좋아","en":"in God's name","n":1,"first":["c6-l6",0]},{"lem":"im stand","t":"im Stande","ko":"~할 수 있는","en":"able to","n":1,"first":["c7-l7",1]},{"lem":"in ordnung","t":"in Ordnung","ko":"괜찮은, 정리된","en":"in order","n":1,"first":["c7-l7",1]},{"lem":"alle tag","t":"alle Tage","ko":"날마다","en":"every day","n":4,"first":["c1-l4",1]},{"lem":"ein paar","t":"ein paar","ko":"몇몇의","en":"a few","n":1,"first":["c7-l4",1]},{"lem":"ein wenig","t":"ein wenig","ko":"조금","en":"a little","n":3,"first":["c1-l5",1]},{"lem":"auf der","t":"auf den","ko":"그래서 ~하도록 (옛말)","en":"so that","n":11,"first":["c1-l3",2]},{"lem":"um uhr","t":"um Uhr","ko":"~시에","en":"at … o'clock","note_ko":"시각 앞의 um 은 ‘~시에’ 예요 (um 6 Uhr = 6시에).","note_en":"Um before a clock time means “at” (um 6 Uhr = at six).","n":6,"first":["c3-l4",0]},{"lem":"ander tag","t":"andern Tag","ko":"다음 날","en":"the next day","note_ko":"am andern Tag = ‘그다음 날’ (옛 철자 andern) 이에요.","note_en":"Am andern Tag means “on the next day”.","n":4,"first":["c4-l1",1]},{"lem":"ich versichern sie","t":"ich versichere Sie","ko":"당신께 장담해요","en":"I assure you","note_ko":"편지에 자주 쓰는 다짐 ‘장담하건대’ 예요.","note_en":"A letter formula: “I assure you”.","n":3,"first":["c3-l6",2]},{"lem":"lob und dank","t":"Lob und Dank","ko":"찬양과 감사","en":"praise and thanks","note_ko":"Gott Lob und Dank = ‘하느님께 찬양과 감사를’ (다행히) 이에요.","note_en":"Gott Lob und Dank = “praise and thanks be to God” (thankfully).","n":3,"first":["c1-l2",0]},{"lem":"vor jahr","t":"vor Jahren","ko":"몇 해 전","en":"years ago","note_ko":"vor Jahren = ‘몇 해 전에’ 예요.","note_en":"Vor Jahren means “years ago”.","n":3,"first":["p2",0]},{"lem":"bei hof","t":"bei Hof","ko":"궁정에서","en":"at court","note_ko":"bei Hof = ‘궁정에서’ (임금 · 제후의 곁) 예요.","note_en":"Bei Hof means “at court”.","n":3,"first":["c2-l5",0]},{"lem":"in der welt","t":"in der Welt","ko":"세상에서","en":"in the world","n":3,"first":["c4-l4",3]},{"lem":"von der welt","t":"von der Welt","ko":"세상의","en":"of the world","n":3,"first":["c4-l5",4]}]}
